we should kill them  we can murder the man but what about the  movement brother  martyrs tend to have a long half-life  hey guys pete here today i'm going to be  talking about the new official trailer  that just came out for the apple tv  series based on isaac asimov's classic  sci-fi series foundation there isn't a  ton of brand new footage in it there are  a couple of things and i do think we get  a better idea of what to expect from the  series overall for a spoiler warning as  someone who's read all of asimov's  foundation series plus the robots and  empire books i will be referring to  those but i won't be giving away any  spoilers about the big twists or how  things end i'll just be sticking to  background information to give you a  better idea of what we can expect and  with that out of the way let's get into  it  the first two episodes of foundation  will be airing in about a month on  friday september 24th and then the  additional episodes will air weekly as  far as what the official trailer shows  us i think there's a few things going on  here first the core of the beginning of  the original trilogy that centers around  harry selden and galdornik is there  in case you've never read any of the  original stories i'll give you the brief  rundown harry selden who's played by  jared harris here has developed  psycho-history a mathematical  statistical science that incorporates  history psychology and sociology to  predict future events based on the  behaviors of large populations of people  in his work he's discovered that the  galactic empire which has ruled for more  than 10 000 years will fall and then  that's going to be followed by a long  period of chaos  because the ruling class doesn't want to  give up their power it's in their  interest not to believe him and  generally they don't want to hear about  his predictions  as far as the collapse things are too  far along to stop it selden's plan is to  create the foundation in an effort to  shorten the inner regnum and help usher  in the new galactic empire in the next  1000 years this would be a big  improvement over the 30 000 years of  chaos that was originally predicted he's  recruited gal dornick a mathematician  from a provincial world to help  implement the psycho-historian's plan  most of what you've seen in the teasers  between harry and gal is taken directly  from the first chapter of the book  foundation and it's expanded on in this  official trailer it's a big deal for gal  or anyone from her planet to visit  trantor to even travel there and she's  got a job and when she arrives to work  for this famous mathematician she finds  out that his work isn't theoretical that  psycho history is real where it looks  like they've changed this some is that  they're just going to give us more  information about what happened both of  these characters only show up at the  beginning and there's a 50 year time  jump that happens right after some of  this could be from that time and then  some of it will likely be there to make  it work better as a tv drama and i'll  come back to that in a minute the second  thing that jumps right out at you is  that there is a lot of action sequences  and i think it's worth mentioning that  they look pretty amazing ships in orbit  planets under attack people charging  across what look like battlefields  firing weapons it all gives you the  impression that this is a high-paced  series that's filled with intense  battles and impressive set pieces the  book series isn't known for this kind of  stuff in fact the lack of action is one  of the things that made it seem like it  would be a hard adaptation  some of what you see in the trailer may  be pulling from things that happen off  screen in the books but even if that's  the case it looks like there'll be a lot  more of a focus on that and we'll have  to wait and see how that all works out  the third thing that stands out is that  there are some things here that seem to  be pulled from the prequels although to  me it looks like they're pulling them  forward in the timeline so that they  occur at the same time as the events of  the beginning of the original trilogy  one thing i wasn't sure about when the  last teaser came out was who the actor  alfred enoch was playing since then it's  been confirmed that he's playing rach  selden he plays a big role in the  prequels he was a street kid that harry  came across in some of his adventures on  trantor and then became his adoptive son  but he would have been a lot older by  the time galdornik arrived because at  the end of the prequels 40 years had  passed since harry first met the 12 year  old rach he grew up he got married and  gave harry two grandchildren it doesn't  look like that's going to be the case in  the show and so now let's look at  everything else that stands out as being  new in this official trailer because  part of it is related to him it opens  with a new overhead shot of galdornik's  home planet of synax from this it looks  like it's a planet covered with water  there's several new quick shots of gal  transitioning to life on trantor and in  those it looks like there's going to be  a connection between her and rach they  do share a lot of scenes in the previous  teasers it looked like he was showing  her around but here it looks like  there's a relationship developing you  see them in a scene where she has her  head on his shoulder and says this is  the plan and then you see them kiss that  doesn't really create any problems in  relation to the original story but it  might have implications down the road  without getting into spoilers that might  be part of the reason that harry selden  sticks around in the story for a while  longer which doesn't seem like it'll be  a problem considering most people love  jared harris  another brand new sequence is this one  where the emperor is out there amongst  the people things look pretty destroyed  and that's probably related to one of  the battle scenes that are sprinkled  throughout the trailer in the voice over  you hear the clone emperors talking  about what you presume is harry seldon  and the psycho historians brother dusk  says we should kill them and brother day  responds we can murder the man but what  about the movement brother martyrs tend  to have a long half-life this seems to  be building off what he was saying in  the second teaser that harry had a mast  of following and that there are people  out there that hinge their hopes on  every word that seldon utters so it does  seem like the tension will be increased  in the lead up to the encyclopedist  leaving trantor for terminus and we do  get our first mentions of that in the  voice over here harry says many years  from now if humanity is going to climb  from the ashes the coming generations  will need the knowledge to build upon a  foundation gal continues we must  preserve only the most essential pieces  of civilization deciding what is  remembered what is forgotten that's the  setup for what's to come for when the  series transitions to terminus and it  focuses on the mayor salver hardin now  in my last video i talked more about the  clone situation how that keeps lee pace  in the series longer and about the  changes for the vault and salver harden  so if you haven't seen that you should  check out that video for more  information on those two things in this  trailer we do get a couple of new shots  with salvor at the vault we see her  reaching out to it at one point and in  another it looks like she asks it what's  the plan and then there's this shot of  her in a suit out in the vacuum there's  what looks like a spin station or a ship  and a lot of asteroids which could be  debris i have no idea what's going on  here it doesn't remind me of anything  that happens in harden's parts in the  book and it makes me wonder if they're  combining some characters and events  while rearranging the timeline  it looks kind of cool though and it does  seem to indicate that we'll be jumping  ahead at least 50 years in the first  season  visually this all looks great there's  nothing in this official trailer that's  made me change my mind i'm still feeling  somewhat optimistic about this  i don't think expanding the time we  spend with harry and gal after she  arrives i don't think that sounds like a  bad thing adding some action sequences  always seemed like it might be essential  to attracting a wider audience i'm  definitely in the club that enjoys the  books as they are but can also see that  there are some things that might not  work so well for television in my  thinking a one-to-one adaptation would  be terribly boring for people who hadn't  read the books and it probably wouldn't  get made  however i'm drawn to stories for the  ideas i don't consume a lot of  action-based entertainment and so i hope  they can strike a balance nothing wrong  with tension and some kick-ass stuff to  get the blood pumping if it's done well  but it needs to not overshadow what was  good about these stories in the first  place i don't feel the need to get  worried about it at this point their  trailers of course they're gonna  showcase the most visually stimulating  stuff they need to bring people in  in the trailer breakdown that david s  goyer made where he talks about some of  the challenges he mentions that they  really wanted to take this story that  had fantastic big ideas and then make it  work for tv and a big challenge was how  are they going to make it emotional how  could they make it intimate and we'll  see if they're able to pull that off  another challenge i mentioned is how it  moves through time and this was  addressed in a recent article with  hollywood reporter where he says that he  figured out a way to have some of the  characters extend their life spans about  six characters will continue from season  to season from century to century so  it's half anthology half continuing  story in the original there's two  characters who stay in the story through  the generations in different ways cleon  the clone emperor would be the third  presuming he only counts as one and if  six is the right number then that leaves  three more it makes me wonder seeing all  these different tanks and people being  submerged if there won't be suspended  animation or hibernation involved the  main characters from this season  sticking around to come back later  according to the plan that wouldn't be a  huge stretch and i suppose it's too much  to get into right now but i would just  hope to see that they don't diminish the  way people react to the plan and  experience the future crises and that  seems like a good place to leave things  i'll probably think about this some more  and then do a predictions type of video  before the first episode comes out until  then let me know what you think about  the trailer in the comments and what  you're hoping to see in the series i'm  down if you want to talk book spoilers  just please mark those accordingly we  don't want to spoil future plot points  for people who haven't read the books  i'm really curious to see how they use  ado demmersell in this first season and  if there's going to be any surprises  with that please like this video if you  enjoyed it please do check out my other  foundation videos if you haven't seen  them please subscribe to my channel if  you haven't already and let me know if  you have any questions thanks for  watching i'll talk to you soon

